[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3608634794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3608634794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3608634794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XF2Wq","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T20:07:42Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T20:07:42Z","body":"I'm not quite sure about the [C# errors](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/19906651560/job/57064552192?pr=113524#step:17:89):\r\n```\r\nError: /home/runner/work/godot/godot/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharpEditor/Generated/GodotObjects/EditorFileDialog.cs(101,16):\r\nerror CS0108: 'EditorFileDialog.GetFileMode()' hides inherited member 'FileDialog.GetFileMode()'.\r\nUse the new keyword if hiding was intended. \r\n[/home/runner/work/godot/godot/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharpEditor/GodotSharpEditor.csproj]\r\n```\r\n\r\nDo compatibility methods clash with regular ones?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3608634794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3608710415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3608710415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3608710415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XGI0P","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T20:27:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T20:27:43Z","body":"@raulsntos Do you have any ideas for how to handle the C# issues?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3608710415/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3609146872","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3609146872","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3609146872,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XHzX4","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T22:39:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T22:39:24Z","body":"Hiding inherited methods only happens when both methods have the same signature or only differ by the return type which can't be overloaded. So the only problematic methods are:\r\n\r\n- `int GetFileMode()`\r\n- `int GetDisplayMode()`\r\n- `int GetAccess()`\r\n- `void AddFilter(string filter, string description)`\r\n\r\nIt doesn't seem necessary to add a compat method for `add_filter` since the hash should match, right? There's no enum involved in this method.\r\n\r\nAnd by the way, the getters are returning `int` instead of the enum because the compat enums aren't \"exposed\" (I think you need to add and expose the enum constants).\r\n\r\nBut either way, I don't think there's anything we can do about the getters other than:\r\n\r\n1. Skip these methods in the C# bindings and break compatibility.\r\n2. Use the `new` keyword to silence the warnings, but this will make these compat methods preferred over the base methods from `FileDialog`. It's probably fine since these compat methods are just calling the base methods anyway, but they will return the compat enum and that may result in an annoying user experience of mixing both enum types in different APIs.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3609146872/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3609160698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3609160698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3609160698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XH2v6","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T22:45:35Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T11:07:11Z","body":"If having compat methods will cause too many problems for C#, instead we could add the hashes to `GDExtensionSpecialCompatHashes`?\r\n\r\nThat would fix the issue this PR aims to fix for just GDExtension","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3609160698/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3611740554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3611740554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3611740554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XRsmK","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T11:38:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T11:38:07Z","body":"I applied David's suggestion with the special compat-hash mapping. Seems to work in Rust at least :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> It doesn't seem necessary to add a compat method for `add_filter` since the hash should match, right? There's no enum involved in this method.\r\n\r\n@raulsntos the hash is different, however the regular derived->base lookup seems to work here. I thus removed `add_filter`. Thanks!\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> Assuming you've tested this with godot-rust (using the mode where it loads all methods) and this worked and it didn't turn up any other instances of missing methods - then I think we're good :-)\r\n\r\nI did! Also added [an integration test](https://github.com/godot-rust/gdext/pull/1432) which calls the 3 method pairs, to make sure there's no UB in the hash forwarding. That said, it's a bit of an unusual setup, since the class is only available in the editor... so I hope I didn't miss anything!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3611740554/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3612070670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113524#issuecomment-3612070670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113524","id":3612070670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XS9MO","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.